// `Int / Int` yields `Float`. The REFERENCE emitter lowers it to `f64.div`
// over converted operands since Float became a native f64 value (issue #3295,
// docs/wasm-capabilities.md), instead of the pre-#2201 `i64.div_s` that
// answered `3` where the language says `3.5`.
//
// This document now pins a PORT gap, not a reference refusal: the revl port in
// selfhost/emit_wasm.rvl carries the scalar Int/Bool subset only and names `/`
// as `<<UNSUPPORTED-TRUE-DIVISION:Float>>`. Both positions are here because
// they reach different code: `ratio` is the scalar binding (the port's
// render_bin gap), and `half` is the interpolation (the port refuses
// `<<UNSUPPORTED-EXPR:interp>>` before it reaches the division).
//
// It is not a byte-agreement case, so it cannot live in the tier's CORPUS; the
// reference-side facts (f64.div, never i64.div_s) are asserted by
// tests/test_selfhost_emit_wasm.py::
// test_true_division_lowers_on_the_reference_but_is_a_named_port_gap.
fn ratio(a: Int, b: Int) { return a / b }

fn half(a: Int, b: Int) -> Str { return `${a / b}` }
